# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values from your Supabase
# project: Dashboard → Project Settings → API.
#
# Leave the first two blank and the app runs entirely in the browser with an
# empty register — useful for looking at the screens, but not a shared register.

# --- Safe in a browser -------------------------------------------------------
# The publishable/anon key is designed to be public. What protects the data is
# row-level security in the database (supabase/schema.sql), not secrecy here.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- SERVER ONLY — never expose this -----------------------------------------
# Needed only so a committee admin can create volunteer logins from the Manage
# screen. It bypasses every security policy, so:
#
#   * it has NO `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix, which is what stops Next.js bundling it
#     into code the browser downloads;
#   * it is read only inside src/app/api/staff/route.ts, which runs on a server;
#   * paste it straight into Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables. Don't
#     put it in a chat, a screenshot, or anywhere it gets stored twice.
#
# Find it under Project Settings → API → `service_role` / `secret`.
# Leave it blank and everything works except adding new accounts.

SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
